    {
      "id": "550",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 550,
        "relationship_type": "antonym",
        "body": "はじめる attaches to verb stems to mean 'to begin' or 'start' doing something, e.g. 食べはじめる 'to start eating'. In contrast, てしまう・ちゃう follows the て-form and can express doing something unintentionally or completely, e.g. 食べてしまった・食べちゃった ('I ate it unintentionally.' or 'I ate it all.').",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 115,
          "slug": "はじめる",
          "title": "はじめる",
          "meaning": "To start, To begin to",
          "level": "JLPT4",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
          "id": 172,
          "slug": "てしまう-ちゃう",
          "title": "てしまう・ちゃう",
          "meaning": "To do something by accident, To finish completely・totally, Unfortunately",
          "level": "JLPT4",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "614",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 614,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "ていく expresses either literal movement away from the speaker or a change that begins now and continues into the future. In contrast, はじめる attaches to the verb stem to mean 'to start (A)'. The key difference is nuance: ていく highlights ongoing progression and continuation going forward, while はじめる focuses on the starting point and the idea of commencing an action.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 137,
          "slug": "ていく",
          "title": "ていく",
          "meaning": "To ~ and go, To go on, To start",
          "level": "JLPT4",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
          "id": 115,
          "slug": "はじめる",
          "title": "はじめる",
          "meaning": "To start, To begin to",
          "level": "JLPT4",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "549",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 549,
        "relationship_type": "antonym",
        "body": "はじめる and おわる can be attached to the stem of verbs to express the contrasting ideas of 'beginning' and 'finishing' an action, respectively. For example, 読みはじめる means 'to begin reading', while 読みおわる means 'to finish reading'.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 115,
